Create one production-ready, universal frame asset for the Urkaaaz match HUD.
The exact same asset must be suitable for the three bottom dock panels
(Supply/units/orders, ammunition, spells/Mana), both fortress HP cards, and the
central timer panel. Do not create a screen mockup or separate component
variants.

## Reference inputs

Attach:

1. A current Urkaaaz match-screen screenshot showing the bottom command dock,
   both fortress HP cards, and the central timer panel.
2. The latest user-supplied square gold frame image as a reference for the
   stronger metallic border and gold material only. Ignore its dark center,
   square composition, and chamfered corners. Adapt the border to a horizontal
   rounded-rectangle panel with a fully transparent center.
3. Do not attach `health_card_frame.png`; its dark fill could bias the result
   toward an opaque black panel.
4. An approved Urkaaaz Loadout or campaign UI reference if further material
   guidance is needed.

Do not use the current slot-frame asset or the old dock-group frame as style
references.

Preserve the reference game's painted fantasy identity. Do not reproduce
specific labels, icons, unit art, or a complete screen.

## Output

- Filename: `match_hud_universal_frame.png`
- Source path: `assets_src/match/hud/match_hud_universal_frame.png`
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 190 pixels (approximately 2.7:1 landscape). Do not
  return a square image, a padded square canvas, or a frame occupying only a
  small part of the canvas.
- Format: RGBA PNG.
- Produce exactly one standalone asset.
- Keep a low-detail horizontal and vertical center suitable for Nine-patch
  stretching. Do not include Nine-patch guide pixels or markers.

## Design

Create a horizontal rounded-rectangle frame for a landscape mobile game HUD.
Use a clearly visible, substantial bronze-gold metallic border with warm
highlights and shallow depth, guided by the latest user-supplied frame image.
The sample is a material reference only: do not copy its square composition,
dark center, or clipped corner shape. The outer and inner frame contours must
turn through smooth, continuous rounded arcs. Do not use diagonal corner cuts,
chamfers, polygonal corners, or angular shoulders.

The same frame will be Nine-patch resized across differently proportioned
targets: three broad bottom panels around 108 dp high, two compact HP cards
around 42 dp high, and the central timer/wind/pause panel. Preserve the curved
corners and border thickness while allowing only straight edge sections and
the plain center to stretch. Keep the corner treatment compact enough to
remain balanced on the shorter HP and timer panels.

Keep the entire panel interior fully transparent (alpha 0): do not fill it
with black, near-black, gray, or any other color. Only the metallic frame
pixels may have visible alpha. Do not simulate transparency with a black
background. The Android UI supplies a separate `#1A1A1A` underlay at 80%
opacity (`#CC` alpha) beneath the frame; do not bake it
into the PNG. Keep the metal finish clean and consistent; this is a reusable
frame, not a focal illustration. Use one symmetric treatment that works for
left, center, and right placement.

The frame must remain visually suitable around all of these targets without
signaling one team or HUD section over another:

- the Supply/units/orders panel;
- the ammunition panel;
- the spells/Mana panel;
- the blue fortress HP card;
- the red fortress HP card;
- the central timer, wind, and pause panel.

## Runtime content — do not bake into the image

Android renders all labels, icons, timer digits, wind indicator, pause control,
HP values and bars, slot states, resource meters, and interaction feedback
above this frame. Do not include or imply a
specific resource, team, unit, ammunition, spell, selection, or gameplay state.
Use the same PNG for every target; do not add dividers or details that force
a specific group layout. Do not bake a drop shadow into the PNG; the HUD adds a
soft native shadow programmatically.

## Negative requirements

- No text, numbers, labels, icons, symbols, button shapes, slot dividers, meter,
  progress fill, or team coloring.
- No unit, spell, ammunition, Supply crate, Mana orb, battlefield, screenshot,
  device frame, logo, watermark, signature, or contact sheet.
- No opaque rectangular canvas background: pixels outside the rounded panel
  silhouette must be fully transparent.
- No fill or texture in the panel interior; every interior pixel must have
  zero alpha.
- No square composition, oversized transparent margins, or a small frame
  centered inside the 512 x 190 canvas.
- No chamfered, clipped, beveled-diagonal, or polygonal outer corners.
- No bulky ornament, spikes, large rivets, excessive glow, neon, busy texture,
  or bright details that compete with dynamic controls.
- No uneven corners, asymmetric frame, jagged edge, or details that distort
  when the center stretches.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the output is one valid 512 x 190 RGBA PNG with the exact filename.
- Confirm both the exterior and the panel interior are transparent.
- Confirm the metallic frame is visibly stronger than the previous delicate
  line and the panel does not read as a black-filled card.
- Preview the same asset around all three bottom panels, both HP cards, and
  the central timer panel. Include both short and wide aspect ratios.
- Confirm the same frame looks proportionate on the 108 dp dock groups and
  the approximately 42 dp HP cards without changing corner shape or border
  thickness.
- Do not integrate it into Android resources until approved.
